course: dictionary
lesson: 10622
title: Unfamiliar words and places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unfamiliar means not known to you, or not seen before. «Big changes, like moving house, starting a new school or a new year group, feel strange at first because everything is unfamiliar.» The sentence tells you why these changes feel strange: everything is new to you.
explain: You can be unfamiliar with a thing, a place, a face or a word. Being unfamiliar with something means you do not know much about it. «I am unfamiliar with this game» means you have not played it much.
explain: The sentence also gives clues about what to do. It says that knowing what to expect, keeping usual routines and giving yourself time make things feel normal again. So feeling unfamiliar is normal, and it gets easier as things become familiar.
fact: Unfamiliar means not known to you or not seen before.
fact: «Unfamiliar with something» means you do not know much about it.
fact: In reading, look up unfamiliar words in a dictionary, or use the context to guess their meaning first.
fact: Feeling unsure in an unfamiliar place is normal, and it often fades with time.
fact: Safety rule: be careful with unfamiliar people, and never go anywhere with a stranger.
exercise: «Starting a new school can feel strange because everything is unfamiliar.» What does unfamiliar mean here? | Loud and noisy | *Not known to you yet | Happy and bright | Very large and grand
exercise: Sam says, «I am unfamiliar with this game.» What does that tell you? | He does not like games | *He does not know much about the game | He has played it every day for years | He is winning the game
exercise: Which word means not known to you or not seen before? | familiar | *unfamiliar | ancient | curt
test: «Going into an unfamiliar place, Ella held her dad's hand.» What does this suggest about Ella? | She knows every corner of the place | *She does not know the place yet, so she may feel unsure | She is bored and sleepy | She has lost her dad
test: Why should you be careful with unfamiliar people? | Because they are always very tall | *Because you do not know them yet | Because they are always kind | Because they live nearby
exam: What helps you feel less unfamiliar with a new school? | *Knowing what to expect, keeping usual routines and giving yourself time | Telling everyone you are fine without trying | Skipping every routine and changing everything at once | Never going in at all
